title: "ASymCat: Asymmetric measures of association between categorical variables"
abstract: >-
  ASymCat is a Python library for obtaining symmetric and asymmetric measures of
  association between categorical variables in data exploration and description.
  It provides directional (X->Y and Y->X) probabilistic, information-theoretic,
  and statistical measures behind a single consistent interface, with robust
  smoothing, bias-corrected entropy estimation, significance testing, and
  confidence intervals.
